\title{dotlinplot: Faithful Plots of Zero-Inflated Single-Cell Expression}
\description{
Dotlin plots show zero-inflated distributions, such as single-cell gene expression, faithfully by separating two pieces of information: the proportion of cells in which a gene is detected, drawn as a bar below zero, and the distribution of the non-zero values, drawn as a violin with jittered points. Works with 'Seurat' and 'SingleCellExperiment' objects and with plain data frames.
